            "best_answer": true,
            "best_answer_content": "Hello,\n\nI think you are talking about STM32H7 dual core that has that restriction in SMPS mode:\n\n![SMPS usage restriction from the DS.png](https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/27f24835-f121-bd18-9d4b-6f52e94c45df.png \"SMPS usage restriction from the DS.png\")\n\nBut STM32H723 doesn't have such restriction in SMPS mode:\n\n![mALLEm_0-1776260154680.png](https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/f22aef46-7816-71c2-e669-6cfb233e001e.png \"mALLEm_0-1776260154680.png\")\n\nSee also FAQ: [Why the DIRECT\\_SMPS\\_SUPPLY option is not shown in STM32CubeMX for STM32H7 MCUs](https://community.st.com/t5/stm32-mcus/faq-why-the-direct-smps-supply-option-is-not-shown-in/ta-p/853623)",
            "best_answer_author": "mƎALLEm",
            "best_answer_author_role": "ST Technical Moderator",
            "content_text": "Hi,\n\nPlanning to use VFQFPN68 package. I am confused about the max core clock I can use. CubeMx shows 550MHz for every \"Power Regulator Voltage Scale (0-3)\".\n\nI remember reading VFQFPN68 has only DCDC solution so max core clock is 400MHz\n\nCan anyone explain please?\n\nThanks,\n\nTim",
            "images": [
                "https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/f22aef46-7816-71c2-e669-6cfb233e001e.png",
                "https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/a55b4bcd-5e9c-1964-5e34-cc5c0e3ebcab.png",
                "https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/27f24835-f121-bd18-9d4b-6f52e94c45df.png",
                "https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/a05144d8-8a9a-b32e-83a5-9bd2f3977e33.png"
            ],
